WEBVTT

00:00.223 --> 00:02.230
- [Instructor] We are told
the differentiable functions

00:02.230 --> 00:06.323
X and Y are related by
the following equation,

00:06.323 --> 00:09.388
Y is equal to square root of X.

00:09.388 --> 00:10.565
And it's interesting, they're telling us

00:10.565 --> 00:12.742
that they are both
differentiable functions,

00:12.742 --> 00:16.541
even X is a function, must be
a function of something else.

00:16.541 --> 00:18.522
Well, they tell us that
the derivative of X

00:18.522 --> 00:20.439
with respect to T is 12

00:21.319 --> 00:24.119
and they want us to
find the derivative of Y

00:24.119 --> 00:28.093
with respect to T when X is equal to nine.

00:28.093 --> 00:30.237
So, let's just make sure
we can understand this.

00:30.237 --> 00:34.214
So, they're telling us that
both X and Y are functions.

00:34.214 --> 00:36.553
Arguably they are both functions of T.

00:36.553 --> 00:38.097
Y is a function of X

00:38.097 --> 00:39.602
but then X is a function of T

00:39.602 --> 00:41.874
so Y could also be a function of T.

00:41.874 --> 00:43.668
One way to think about it is

00:43.668 --> 00:45.668
if X is equal to F of T,

00:47.764 --> 00:51.180
then Y is equal to the square root of X

00:51.180 --> 00:53.430
which would just be F of T.

00:55.273 --> 00:56.696
Another way to think about it

00:56.696 --> 00:58.722
if you took T as your input

00:58.722 --> 01:00.671
into your function F,

01:00.671 --> 01:02.838
you're going to produce X

01:02.838 --> 01:04.578
and then if you took that as your input

01:04.578 --> 01:06.995
into the square root function

01:08.162 --> 01:10.941
you are going to produce Y.

01:10.941 --> 01:14.811
So, you could just view this
as just one big box here,

01:14.811 --> 01:16.894
that Y is a function of Y

01:18.420 --> 01:21.459
but now let's actually
answer their question.

01:21.459 --> 01:24.637
To tackle it we just have
to apply the chain rule.

01:24.637 --> 01:28.316
The chain rule tells us
that the derivative of Y

01:28.316 --> 01:30.242
with respect to T

01:30.242 --> 01:33.054
is going to be equal
to the derivative of Y

01:33.054 --> 01:36.637
with respect to X times
the derivative of X

01:37.539 --> 01:39.675
with respect to T.

01:39.675 --> 01:42.769
So, let's apply it to
this particular situation.

01:42.769 --> 01:45.428
We're gonna have the derivative of Y

01:45.428 --> 01:47.239
with respect to T

01:47.239 --> 01:49.822
is equal to the derivative of Y

01:50.759 --> 01:52.503
with respect to X.

01:52.503 --> 01:53.745
Well, what's that?

01:53.745 --> 01:55.843
Well, Y is equal to the
principle root of X.

01:55.843 --> 01:57.182
You could also write this as Y

01:57.182 --> 01:59.757
is equal to X to the one half power.

01:59.757 --> 02:01.380
We could just use the power rule.

02:01.380 --> 02:03.318
The derivative of Y with respect to X

02:03.318 --> 02:07.233
is one half X to the negative one half.

02:07.233 --> 02:08.766
So, let me write that down.

02:08.766 --> 02:11.683
One half X to the negative one half

02:12.903 --> 02:16.467
and then times the derivative of X

02:16.467 --> 02:19.085
with respect to T times
the derivative of X

02:19.085 --> 02:21.356
with respect to T.

02:21.356 --> 02:24.255
Well, let's see, we wanna find
what we have here in orange,

02:24.255 --> 02:25.772
that's what the questions asks us.

02:25.772 --> 02:28.196
They tell us when X is equal to nine

02:28.196 --> 02:29.385
and the derivative of X

02:29.385 --> 02:30.986
with respect to T is equal to 12.

02:30.986 --> 02:32.685
So, we have all of the information

02:32.685 --> 02:34.604
necessary to solve for this.

02:34.604 --> 02:38.021
So, this is going to be equal to one half

02:39.205 --> 02:42.322
times nine to the negative one half,

02:42.322 --> 02:44.205
nine to the negative one half,

02:44.205 --> 02:48.372
times DX/DT, the derivative
of X with respect to T

02:49.501 --> 02:51.584
is equal to 12, times 12.

02:52.766 --> 02:55.376
So, let's see, nine to the one half

02:55.376 --> 02:56.671
would be three,

02:56.671 --> 03:00.001
nine to the negative
one half would be 1/3,

03:00.001 --> 03:01.493
so this is 1/3,

03:01.493 --> 03:05.660
so this will all simplify
to 1/2 times 1/3 is 1/6,

03:07.839 --> 03:10.122
so we could have a six in the denominator

03:10.122 --> 03:14.357
and then we are going to
have a 12 in the numerator.

03:14.357 --> 03:19.114
So, 12/6, so the derivative
of Y with respect to T

03:19.114 --> 03:20.300
when X is equal to nine

03:20.300 --> 03:23.658
and derivative of X with
respect to 12 is two.
